WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.025
Check yourself with two questions.

2
00:00:02.025 --> 00:00:06.075
First: the smoke test runs on
fixtures with the fixture option.

3
00:00:06.075 --> 00:00:08.162
Can its report promote to production?

4
00:00:08.162 --> 00:00:09.999
The answer is b: no.

5
00:00:09.999 --> 00:00:13.660
Production's pre-flight check
needs a live, passing test run,

6
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:16.938
and a fixture record proves
nothing about the stage.

7
00:00:16.938 --> 00:00:19.838
You saw P F ten refuse it in step six.

8
00:00:19.838 --> 00:00:23.637
Second: rollback add writes an
evidence record for a step.

9
00:00:23.637 --> 00:00:26.374
Why does the evidence check
still mark that row missing?

10
00:00:26.374 --> 00:00:28.791
The answer is a: the record is recorded,

11
00:00:28.791 --> 00:00:33.000
which proves the change was written
down, not that the step worked.

12
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:36.900
That's why only two of seventeen
rows were evidenced in step five.

13
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:41.168
The module page has two more questions,
on the three identities and on what

14
00:00:41.168 --> 00:00:45.980
production's pre-flight check compares,
each linked to the section that answers it.
